Input: {"question": "Which sports team does Sergio González Soriano represent or represent?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 27, "text": "**Sergio González Soriano**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 29, "end": 215, "text": "Sergio González Soriano is a Spanish association football player and manager who currently plays for Guizhou Renhe F.C., a professional association football club based in Beijing, China."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 216, "end": 232, "text": "**Early Career**"}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 234, "end": 351, "text": "Born on August 10, 1985, in Madrid, Spain, Soriano began his football career at the youth academy of Atlético Madrid."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 352, "end": 453, "text": "He quickly rose through the ranks, making his professional debut for the club's reserve team in 2003."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 454, "end": 572, "text": "Over the next five years, Soriano played for various Spanish clubs, including Real Valladolid and Racing de Santander."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 573, "end": 590, "text": "**Move to China**"}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 592, "end": 673, "text": "In 2010, Soriano made the surprise move to China, signing with Guizhou Renhe F.C."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 674, "end": 814, "text": "The move was seen as a significant coup for the Chinese club, which was looking to bolster its squad with experienced international players."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 815, "end": 925, "text": "Since joining Guizhou Renhe, Soriano has become a key player for the team, scoring 23 goals in 75 appearances."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 926, "end": 952, "text": "**Studies and References